# CMake / build output
build/
build-*/
# build_web with an UNDERSCORE is what scripts/build_web.ps1 actually defaults
# to, while the rule above uses a hyphen and README documents the hyphen form.
# The two documented workflows disagreed on exactly the boundary that matters,
# so a web build placed jc_reborn.js, .data and index.html straight into
# `git status` as untracked files.
build_web/
out/
cmake-build-*/
CMakeFiles/
CMakeCache.txt
cmake_install.cmake
Makefile.cmake
# Compiled objects / binaries
*.o
*.obj
*.a
*.lib
*.so
*.dylib
*.exe
*.out
# Emscripten / web
*.wasm
*.bc
# Visual Studio (cache only — committed vs/ project files are kept)
.vs/
*.user
*.suo
# MSBuild writes here; *.exe was already covered but its companions were not.
vs/bin/
vs/publish/
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.exp

# Game data (assets/scrantic_data.zip) is intentionally committed — art reworked / owned.

# AI agent files — never track (local-only / extension-injected)
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
GEMINI.md
KILO.md
.github/copilot-instructions.md
.cursorrules
.windsurfrules
.clinerules
.codex/
SESSION_*
# .claude/ holds per-machine session and worktree state. It was the one hole in
# this list: empty today, so git never surfaced it, and it would have appeared as
# untracked the first time a tool wrote settings into it.
.claude/
